Rae (Presales): Need a tiny POC cheat for tomorrow's demo. Requirements: streaming SDK quickstart (Node + Go), a function/tool-call pattern that validates structured JSON output, ephemeral token handshake cURL, short security bullets (KMS, retention, SOC2 link), and two pricing options (reserved vs payg placeholders). Can someone drop a one-screen draft?

Omar (Eng): I got this. Confirm hosted EU region and ephemeral tokens? Any latency SLOs to call out?

Priya (Sales): Hosted EU, aim is 99p <200ms. They want logs off by default and an explicit fallback to a quantized model for cost spikes. Finance will fill $ placeholders.

Omar (Eng): Draft (compact):
- Goal: demo streaming chat with function calls + schema validation.
- Env: hosted (eu), primary r-infer-2, fallback r-infer-2-quant-small.
- Auth: short-lived token or API key. KMS for key storage; TLS required. Logs off by default; retention configurable. SOC2 link to be added by compliance.

Node example (stream + function call):
```js
// Node minimal
const c = new Redwood({ token: process.env.RW_TOKEN, region: 'eu' });
const s = c.chat.stream({ model: 'r-infer-2' });
s.on('event', e => {
  if (e.type === 'function_call') {
    // quick schema check
    if (e.schemaHash !== 'sha256:abc') return;
    fetch('https://hooks.customer/do', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(e.payload) });
  }
});
```

Go example (stream receive):
```go
cli := redwood.NewClient(os.Getenv("RW_TOKEN"))
stream := cli.ChatStream(ctx, redwood.ChatParams{Model: "r-infer-2", Region: "eu"})
for ev := range stream.Events() {
  if ev.Type == redwood.EventFunctionCall && ev.SchemaHash == "sha256:abc" {
    http.Post("https://hooks.customer/do", "application/json", bytes.NewReader(ev.Payload))
  }
}
```

Handshake cURL (SSE):
```bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $RW_TOKEN" -H "Accept: text/event-stream" \
  "https://api.redwood.ai/v1/streams/chat?model=r-infer-2&region=eu"
```

Operational knobs: batching window 10-20ms, enable KV prefix caching. Fallback policy: if queuing latency >80ms or GPU pool >75% -> route to r-infer-2-quant-small in same region.

Security bullets: EU-only endpoints for POC; TLS in transit & KMS-managed keys at rest (HSM optional); logs non-persistent by default; SOC2 attestation link pending. Incident contact: secops@redwood.ai.

Pricing (placeholders): 1) Reserved capacity + burst bucket (better unit cost) -> $<FINANCE_FILL>; 2) Pay-as-you-go hosted -> $<FINANCE_FILL>.

Troubleshooting quick hits: 401 -> check token exchange/clock skew; SSE stall -> missing Accept header/CORS; webhook failures -> check TLS cert and IP allowlist.

Priya (Sales): I'll chase finance and compliance for SOC2 and numbers. Rae please review and tag @Rae when ready.

